[C5.2] How does Brand Concierge trigger follow-up journeys in Adobe Journey Optimizer?
  conn=ajo+bc lines=["F02","JO02","JO05","JO06"]
  approach=["Adobe's product page describes Journey Optimizer follow-up after concierge conversations, but Experience League documents no setup. The documented follow-up routes today are the handoff to sales and Marketo Engage.","Not a documented capability: a visitor who showed intent in a concierge conversation could get a follow-up by email, SMS or other channels, if Adobe confirms a route for you."]
  cautions=["documents no setup","Not a documented capability"]

[C5.2] How does Brand Concierge use AEM Sites for product cards in answers?
  conn=aemsites+bc lines=["AXE03","F02","SI02","SI01"]
  approach=["Brand Concierge has a native AEM Sites knowledge source: for AEM Sites as a Cloud Service with Content AI enabled, the concierge answers from an existing Content AI index, and Content AI Search is among the integrations Adobe recommends for the Site Advisory skill.","The concierge answers from the AEM Sites content in the Content AI index, without uploads in Brand Concierge; how current it stays depends on how that index is kept up to date."]
  cautions=[]

[C5.2] How does Brand Visibility enrich product detail pages in Adobe Commerce?
  conn=bv+commerce lines=["C02","L02","L03","C07"]
  approach=["Brand Visibility compares the Commerce catalog with what AI agents can read on each product page, then serves the AI assistants Adobe supports (ChatGPT, Perplexity and Claude) the missing details at the CDN through Optimize at Edge. The catalog, and the page shoppers and search engines see, stay unchanged.","The AI assistants Adobe supports (ChatGPT, Perplexity and Claude) get the variants, specifications and attributes the catalog already holds, without a change to the storefront or the catalog; shoppers and search engines see the page as published."]
  cautions=["pilot"]

